\0
In 2598, the Imperium developed an experimental atmospheric processing device in order to accelerate the development of habitable ecosystems. When tested, however, the device malfunctioned and caused catastrophic biological devastation on the trial world of Perlen, and the planet was quarantined.\n\n
Over a century later, the Freedom Guard landed on the planet's surface and determined that Perlen's atmosphere had recovered to a state where it could support life. They intended to establish a clandestine base there, believing that the Imperium would continue to ignore the planet. However, the Imperium had similar ideas and had already begun constructing fortifications on Perlen. The Freedom Guard landing party clashed with Imperium forces already on the planet.
\1
Scout the surface of the planet for a Freedom Guard detachment. An expeditionary force of the insurgents is attempting to establish a base on Perlen.  Fortify your own position, then destroy the fledgling outpost.
\n\n
\cOBJECTIVES\n
\n
--> Establish a base\n
--> Construct five Plasma Turrets\n
--> Destroy all Freedom Guard structures
\2
You learn quickly. Continue on this path, and all will be revealed to you.\n
\n
\cHISTORICAL OUTCOME:\n
The Imperium force was surprised by a larger Freedom Guard scouting company and was quickly overwhelmed. Unable to contact their troops on the planet, the Imperium assumed that Perlen’s atmosphere remained toxic and suspended investigation. The Imperium did not discover the Freedom Guard base established on the planet until many years later.
\3
I fear you lack the strength to achieve what is necessary.

